  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Score, label, alert",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Three different things, and collapsing them is what produces alert storms.\n\n- **Score** is continuous: how far from baseline, in sigma.\n- **Label** is the binary judgement after a threshold.\n- **Alert** is what reaches a human, after duration, minimum volume, maintenance suppression, severity and deduplication.\n\nThe scorecard is measured against known incidents. **Event recall** is the share of incidents caught at least once; **alerts/day** is what your on-call rota has to absorb. Moving a threshold trades one for the other, and there is no setting that wins both."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Event recall",
      "description": "Share of known incidents caught at least once. The headline number.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(aiops_python_result{column=\"eval_event_recall\"})",
          "legendFormat": "Event recall",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
